<article class="env-definition" id="0DN1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DN1">Definition <span data-tag="0DN1">72.17.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper algebraic over $k$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. In this situation the <em>Euler characteristic of $\mathcal{F}$</em> is the integer </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \chi (X, \mathcal{F}) = \sum \nolimits _ i (-1)^ i \dim _ k H^ i(X, \mathcal{F}).  \]
</div>
  <p> For justification of the formula see below. </p>
</article>